\lceil{x}\rceil^2 &\text{if }x\text{ is irrational}.
\end{cases}
\] we need to evaluate \(f(\sqrt[3]{-8})+f(-\pi)+f(\sqrt{50})+f\left(\frac{9}{2}\right)\). Here, \(\sqrt[3]{-8} = -2\), which is rational. So, \(f(\sqrt[3]{-8}) = | \lfloor -2 \rfloor | = | -2 | = 2 \). Next, \(-\pi\) is irrational. So, \(f(-\pi) = \lceil -\pi \rceil^2 = \lceil -3.14159 \rceil^2 = (-3)^2 = 9 \). Next, \(\sqrt{50}\) is irrational. So, \(f(\sqrt{50}) = \lceil \sqrt{50} \rceil^2 = \lceil 7.071 \rceil^2 = 8^2 = 64 \). Finally, \(\frac{9}{2} = 4.5\) is rational. So, \(f\left(\frac{9}{2}\right) = \left| \lfloor 4.5 \rfloor \right| = |4| = 4 \). Adding these together, we get \(2 + 9 + 64 + 4 = 79 \). </think> <answer>79</answer>

